license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/kaganyurtk/sparse-trajectory-reconstruction"
url: "https://github.com/kaganyurtk/sparse-trajectory-reconstruction"
abstract: >-
  Reproducibility materials for matched unconstrained and kinematically
  constrained neural-network studies of sparse rocket-trajectory
  reconstruction. The package contains the complete RQ1 Falcon 9 training,
  validation, and held-out evaluation code together with safe RQ2 FlightSketch
  data-curation and split-preparation utilities. Third-party telemetry,
  processed trajectories, trained weights, and the unavailable historical RQ2
  model-fitting runner are not included.
keywords:
  - rocket telemetry
  - trajectory reconstruction
  - physics-informed machine learning
  - kinematic constraints
  - sparse observations
  - reproducibility
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: "When kinematic constraints conflict with rocket telemetry: sparse trajectory reconstruction across two real-flight datasets"
